Third-party dependencies (installed from PyPI, not redistributed in this repository)

- GUDHI (https://gudhi.inria.fr), MIT overall. Its AlphaComplex module (gudhi/delaunay_complex.py) and its
  bottleneck distance (gudhi/bottleneck.py) declare GPL-3.0 because they build on CGAL. This repository's own
  source code stays MIT; anyone who redistributes a combined binary that includes these GUDHI modules must
  follow GPL-3.0.
- ripser.py and persim (scikit-tda), MIT. persim is installed as a dependency of ripser.py and DREiMac.
- DREiMac (scikit-tda), Apache-2.0.
- The git submodule external/shape-fitting (BurnyCoder/shape-fitting-in-neural-geometry-in-llm-mechanistic-interpretability), MIT.
